## A. Using this

The runbook for setting {{ project_name }} up for somebody.

1. **Ask first.** Before installing anything, ask what the person wants to do with it and
   which of the steps below they already have.
2. **Install the tools:** {% if python %}`uv` and {% endif %}`pre-commit`
   (`uv tool install pre-commit`).
3. **Set up:** `make setup`. It {% if python %}creates the environment with `uv sync` and {% endif %}installs the git hooks.
4. **Cheapest run:** `make check`. Green means the checkout matches what CI sees.

`make help` lists every target.

## B. Changing the code

### How a change moves

1. **Branch.** Off `main`, one branch and one worktree per writer. Rendered output (a PDF,
   an image, a built page) goes to `out/` in the person's main checkout, never only into a
   worktree, so there is one place to look. A long-running process (a loop, a server) runs
   from its own checkout.
2. **One milestone.** One logical change, a test that fails without it, `make check`, one
   commit. Small and buildable, not a day-long branch.
3. **Show it.** Run the change for real once. Until then it is listed in
   `.agent/DEFERRED_VERIFICATION.md`.
4. **Route what is not the task.** Anything noticed on the way goes to a ledger, not into
   this change.
5. **Integrate.** Up to date with `main`, `make check`, one independent review pass, then
   at most one recheck; what it finds after that is fixed forward. Open a pull request; the
   person merges it on GitHub. Push only when the person says so; never force-push.
6. **Close.** Once merged: remove the worktree, delete the branch, and in the main checkout
   `git switch main && git pull --ff-only`. Ledgers updated, nothing left open.

### Where each fact lives

One place per fact; no second copy anywhere. A file is created only when it has content.

| Fact | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| Rules, commands, gates, how a change moves | `AGENTS.md` |
| What the thing is for and for whom | `docs/PRODUCT.md`, only if the README does not say it |
| Why it is built the way it is | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Work a person has chosen to do | `docs/BACKLOG.md` |
| Setup, first run, everyday use | `README.md` |
| What changed for users | `CHANGELOG.md` |
| Open observations and proposals | the ledgers in `.agent/` |

### Ledgers

Tracked files in `.agent/`, each created with its first row and listing only what is open:
`FINDINGS.md` (observations outside the task), `DEFERRED_VERIFICATION.md` (commits no
real run has shown working yet), `AGENT_IMPROVEMENTS.md` (proposals for how work here is
done) and `UPSTREAM_ISSUES.md` (external behaviour worked around). An entry grants no new
scope; a person decides. A settled row is deleted in the commit that settles it.

